From: apklayer
Subject: [PATCH] ActivityThread.getApplication() is null while the app's Application is made and attached

On Android mInitialApplication is set by handleBindApplication after LoadedApk.makeApplication returns, so the Application class's static
initializer, its constructor and attachBaseContext see ActivityThread.currentApplication() == null. Robolectric installs a stand-in
Application (package "android", on the system context) before it loads the app's class, then sets the app's own before its attach, and
ShadowActivityThread.getApplication falls back to RuntimeEnvironment.getApplication(). Tencent ACE (PGR) calls getApplication() from
libanogs' JNI_OnLoad, run from the Application's static initializer, and got the stand-in (getFilesDir threw "No data directory found for
package android"). ApklayerBinding.binding (runtime/patches, apklayer's own) now covers that window and getApplication answers null in it;
apklayer's host code that needs the app there uses ApklayerBinding.hostApplication().
Against external/robolectric 87aa52b08 (REVISION), after 0025.
---
--- a/robolectric/src/main/java/org/robolectric/android/internal/AndroidTestEnvironment.java
+++ b/robolectric/src/main/java/org/robolectric/android/internal/AndroidTestEnvironment.java
@@ -296,6 +296,9 @@
     activityThreadReflector.setInitialApplication(dummyInitialApplication);
     ShadowApplication shadowInitialApplication = Shadow.extract(dummyInitialApplication);
     shadowInitialApplication.callAttach(systemContextImpl);
+    // apklayer patch: from here until the app's Application is attached ActivityThread.getApplication() is null, as on Android (ApklayerBinding);
+    // the app's class is initialized in this window (getApplicationClass), its constructor and attachBaseContext run in it
+    ApklayerBinding.binding = true;
 
     Package parsedPackage = loadAppPackage(appManifest);
 
@@ -379,6 +382,7 @@
     activityThreadReflector.setInitialApplication(application);
     ShadowApplication shadowApplication = Shadow.extract(application);
     shadowApplication.callAttach(contextImpl);
+    ApklayerBinding.binding = false;  // apklayer patch: as handleBindApplication's mInitialApplication = app after makeApplication
     reflector(ContextImplReflector.class, contextImpl).setOuterContext(application);
     if (apiLevel >= VERSION_CODES.O) {
       reflector(ContextImplReflector.class, contextImpl)
--- a/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowActivityThread.java
+++ b/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowActivityThread.java
@@ -143,6 +143,10 @@
 
   @Implementation
   protected Application getApplication() {
+    // apklayer patch: null while the app's Application is made and attached, as mInitialApplication on Android (ApklayerBinding)
+    if (org.robolectric.android.internal.ApklayerBinding.binding) {
+      return null;
+    }
     // Prefer the stored application from the real Activity Thread.
     Application currentApplication =
         Reflector.reflector(ActivityThreadReflector.class, realActivityThread)
